    "title": "Police conduct search at Woonsocket park as part of murder investigation - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Shaun Towne ,\n9 hours ago\nWOONSOCKET, R.I. (WPRI) — Woonsocket and Rhode Island State Police were seen investigating at River Island Art Park on Wednesday, and 12 News has confirmed it was related to a recent homicide case.\nWoonsocket Police Chief Thomas Oates said the State Police Dive Team was helping his officers search for evidence in their investigation of the murder of 29-year-old Gabriela Vallejo .\nThe suspect in that case, 30-year-old William Santiago Ramos, was found at the park and arrested after police said he jumped into the Blackstone River while trying to escape.\nVallejo was Santiago Ramos’s girlfriend, according to police, and she was several months pregnant when she was found stabbed to death at a home on Sayles Street on Aug. 6. Investigators believe she died earlier in the week.\nWATCH: Bodycam video shows arrest of Woonsocket man charged in girlfriend’s murder The victim’s family said Vallejo was the “sweetest, most beautiful girl” and also had a 6-year-old daughter who is now in their care.\nSince the investigation remains active, Oates did not disclose what exactly police were looking for on Wednesday.\nSantiago Ramos is charged with domestic murder, as well as obstructing an officer in the execution of duty and failure to notify sex offender’s change of address. He’s currently being held without bail.\nDownload the WPRI 12 and Pinpoint Weather 12 apps to get breaking news and weather alerts.\nWatch 12 News Now on WPRI.com or with the free WPRI 12+ TV app .\nFollow us on social media:\nClose Thanks for signing up!\nWatch for us in your inbox.\nSubscribe Now\nDaily Roundup Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WPRI.com.\n6",
    "summary": "WOONSOCKET, R.I. (WPRI) — Woonsocket and Rhode Island State Police were seen investigating at River Island Art Park on Wednesday, and 12 News has confirmed it was related to a recent homicide case. The suspect in that case, 30-year-old William Santiago Ramos, was found at the park and arrested after police said he jumped into the Blackstone River while trying to escape. Vallejo was Santiago Ramos’s girlfriend, according to police, and she was several months pregnant when she was found stabbed to death at a home on Sayles Street on Aug. 6.",
